<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#mode-dream> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Dream"@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#mode-divination> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko-manifestation> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#mode-symbolic> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko-manifestation> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#ManifestationModeScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#mode-divination> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#Medium> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A medium through which manifestation is asserted to occur — a person, object, place, text, or instrument. A Medium is the vehicle, not the agent; the sacred agent is modeled in iroko-nkisi or iroko-agency. One ManifestationEvent may involve multiple media."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#mode-embodied> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko-manifestation> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#medium-object> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A material object serves as the medium — a consecrated vessel, nganga, otán, or ritual artifact."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#medium-text> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#MediumType> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#mode-embodied> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Manifestation asserted to occur in a physically embodied form distinct from possession — the agent is present as a body, not occupying another's."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko-manifestation> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#imports> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko-core> .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#mode-divination> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Divination"@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko#manifestsThroughMedium> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Associates a ManifestationEvent with a Medium through which manifestation is asserted to occur. The identity of the medium (e.g., a specific person) may carry its own access level if the medium is a community member."@en .
<https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko-manifestation> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> <https://ontology.irokosociety.org/iroko-narrative> .
